# Baked into the bundle by babel-preset-expo. Both are public by construction: the anon key
# ships in every Supabase client and grants nothing on its own -- the Edge Functions mint a
# short-lived ceedo_app JWT per invocation and never use service_role (parent spec §12.5).
#
# The DEVICE's credential is not here. It arrives by enrollment and lives in the Android
# Keystore (src/auth/credential-store.ts).
#
# Local Supabase, from `supabase status`:
# The LAN address of the machine running Supabase, and PORT 56321 -- not the 54321 default.
# supabase/config.toml declares this project's own ports because another Supabase project
# owns the defaults on this machine (see the README). The tablet cannot reach 127.0.0.1
# either: that is the tablet itself. Use the Mac's LAN IP.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<lan-ip>:56321
EXPO_PUBLIC_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJzdXBhYmFzZS1kZW1vIiwicm9sZSI6ImFub24iLCJleHAiOjE5ODM4MTI5OTZ9.CRXP1A7WOeoJeXxjNni43kdQwgnWNReilDMblYTn_I0
